    python design/import_sounds.py --only voice --verify   # + German speech-recognition check

Writes sounds/sw_*.wav (mono 44.1 kHz 16 bit; the announcer too) and music/sw_music1..3 +
sw_menu (stereo). The file names are the ones scripts/sw/audio.lua asks for.

Needs: Python 3 with numpy, ffmpeg (PATH or env FFMPEG). The voices come from ElevenLabs takes
in design/voice_el/<name>.mp3 (announcer "Lola - Modern Agent", units "Mark - Confident and
Striking", eleven_multilingual_v2); a line without a take falls back to Windows WinRT speech
("Microsoft Katja" / "Microsoft Stefan") through the old robot() chain.
Samples come from D:\\Samples (env SW_SAMPLES): Bluezone BC0197/BC0200/BC0214 (royalty-free
sound-effect packs), NI Battery 4 Factory Library, RD-Cinematic drums/hits and the RC
"Cinematic Electronica" loop packs. Nothing from the Celldweller remix stems, no songs.

Music is written as WAV: the engine decodes music with miniaudio, which here is compiled
without stb_vorbis, so an .ogg would not load (MUSIC_EXT below; .mp3 would also work).
"""
